<title>NETHERLANDS: OCE DETAILS INTERIM STOCK DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>OCE DETAILS INTERIM STOCK DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>VENLO, Netherlands 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copier maker Oce-van der Grinten NV said on Thursday it had set its 1996 optional interim stock dividend at one new share per 209 held.</p>
<p>On October 16 the company announced it would pay a 1996 interim cash dividend of 0.90 guilders but added the interim dividend could be taken up in cash or in new shares. The interim dividend will be payable from November 12.</p>
<p>Oce's shares closed at 181.00 guilders on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange on Thursday, up 0.20 from their previous close.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 (fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
